  "description": "OKOHIJ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H80 Cl1 Gd6 N24 O29 1+,4(C2 H3 N1),Cl1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.853-4.999 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 111.27-172.15°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula {Gd6(L)6(CO3)2(CH3OH)2(H2O)3Cl}Cl·4CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
